---
import Legal from '../layouts/Legal.astro'
import Address from '../components/Address.astro'
import { PAGES } from '../data/pages'
import { COMPANY } from '../data/company'
---

<Legal
  page={PAGES.privacy}
  h1="Privacy policy"
  intro="Ferrocast is built to keep your data on your own computer. This page explains the few things that do leave it, where they go and why."
>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Your overlays, alerts, commands, viewer notes and history stay on your computer.</li>
    <li>
      Sign-in tokens for Twitch, YouTube and Kick are stored privately on your computer: in the
      Windows Credential Manager or the Linux keyring, and on macOS in a file only your user account
      can open.
    </li>
    <li>
      Our relay does three jobs: it receives Kick events, handles Kick sign-in, and hosts tip pages.
    </li>
    <li>
      Kick events (including chat) and tip notices wait on the relay only while your app is offline,
      for up to 7 days, and are then deleted. Without Pro, nothing else from your stream is kept.
    </li>
    <li>
      If you use Ferrocast Pro, our relay keeps only what each Pro feature needs to run. It never
      stores your chat. <a href="#pro-data">Every item is listed below</a>.
    </li>
    <li>Payment details stay with the payment provider. We never see card or UPI details.</li>
    <li>This website has no analytics, no tracking cookies and no third-party scripts.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Who is responsible</h2>
  <p>
    {COMPANY.legalName} is responsible for the data described here. Contact us at
    <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The desktop app</h2>
  <p>
    The app runs on your computer. Everything it stores (settings, overlays, alert rules, media,
    commands, the event log, viewer notes and tip history) is saved in a database on your own disk.
    We cannot see it. You can export it or delete it at any time.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you connect Twitch, YouTube or Kick, you sign in on the platform’s own website. The access
    tokens the platform gives back, your OBS password and your Discord webhook are stored privately
    on your computer, never in the database, exports, backups or logs. On Windows they go in the
    Credential Manager and on Linux in the system keyring. On macOS they go in a file in the app’s
    data folder that only your user account can open, not in the macOS Keychain: the app isn’t
    signed with a paid Apple developer certificate, so the Keychain would ask for your login
    password after every update. OBS keeps its own WebSocket password in a file in the same way. The
    app talks to Twitch and YouTube directly from your computer.
  </p>
  <p>
    The app checks for updates by downloading a public release list. That request includes your IP
    address and the app version, as any download does. We do not attach an identifier to it.
  </p>

  <h2>YouTube</h2>
  <!-- prettier-ignore -->
  <p>
    Ferrocast uses YouTube API Services. When you connect YouTube, the app reads your live chat and stream events and carries out the moderation actions you choose, all from your computer. By connecting YouTube you also agree to the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" rel="noopener">Google Privacy Policy</a>. You can disconnect in Settings → Accounts, or revoke Ferrocast’s access at any time on your <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions" rel="noopener">Google account permissions page</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>The Ferrocast relay</h2>
  <p>
    Some things can only reach a public address on the internet, so we run a small relay. It does
    three jobs:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Kick events.</strong> Kick sends follows, subs, chat messages and similar events only
      to a public address. The relay checks each one is really from Kick and forwards it to your app
      straight away. If your app is offline, events wait in a queue for up to 7 days and are then
      deleted. Once delivered, they are gone from the relay.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Kick sign-in.</strong> Kick’s sign-in needs a secret key that cannot ship inside an
      app, so the relay holds it. When you sign in to Kick, and when your sign-in is refreshed, your
      Kick tokens pass through the relay on their way to your app. They are not stored there.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Tip pages.</strong> The relay serves your tip page and receives payment notices from
      Razorpay, Stripe or Ko-fi. See the next section for exactly what that involves.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    If you use Ferrocast Pro, the relay also runs the Pro features you turn on. See
    <a href="#pro-data">what each Pro feature stores</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    The relay also keeps short technical logs (time, request type, an account id, IP address and
    errors) for up to 14 days to keep the service working and safe. These logs never contain chat
    text, tip messages or a tipper’s contact details.
  </p>

  <h2>Tip pages</h2>
  <p>
    Your tip page shows the display name you choose. Your legal name is never shown on your tip page
    or in your alerts. The payment provider’s checkout and receipt show the name on your provider
    account, so use a business or brand name there if you want to keep your own name private.
  </p>
  <p>When a viewer tips, the tip page server receives:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>their IP address, as any website does;</li>
    <li>the name they choose to show, their message and the amount;</li>
    <li>
      the payment status from the provider, which may include the payer’s email address or phone
      number. We use these only to match the payment to the tip.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Card, UPI and bank details are entered on the provider’s own checkout and never reach us. The
    tip notice is forwarded to your app and deleted from the relay once delivered, or after 7 days
    if your app stays offline. The payer’s email address and phone number are never forwarded to you
    and are deleted with the notice.
  </p>

  <h2>Ferrocast Pro</h2>
  <p>
    Pro is not on sale yet. When it is, we will need an email address for your account and will
    receive billing records from Razorpay (what you bought, when, and the payment status, not your
    card or UPI details). We also keep which of your PCs share the subscription (up to 3). The
    details of each Pro feature are below.
  </p>

  <h2 id="pro-data">What each Pro feature stores</h2>
  <p>
    Pro features run on the Ferrocast relay, so each one keeps a little data there. We keep only
    what the feature needs to work, and only while you use it. Nothing here is used for ads or sold.
  </p>
  <p>Three rules apply to all of them:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Chat is never stored.</strong> The cloud bot keeps the last 200 lines of each chat in
      the relay’s memory only, so your phone can show recent chat. It is gone when the relay
      restarts, when you switch the bot off and when you disconnect.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Secrets are sealed.</strong> Platform sign-in tokens and email addresses are encrypted
      with AES-256-GCM before they are saved. Phone sign-ins are kept only as a hash. Backups are
      encrypted on your PC, and we never have the key.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Deleted 30 days after Pro ends</strong>, unless a shorter time is given below. Many
      items can be removed sooner from the app, as noted.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>24/7 cloud bot (Twitch and Kick)</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What:</strong> for each platform, the bot and channel account ids and names, the
      permissions you granted, the platform’s event subscription ids, when it connected, last
      replied and went live, and the last error or refused reply. Your bot settings: commands,
      timers, auto-replies, counter names and values. Counter changes wait until your PC picks them
      up, for 30 days at most.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Sealed:</strong> the sign-in tokens for the bot account and your channel.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Why:</strong> so the bot can answer in your chat while your PC is off.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long:</strong> until you disconnect, when the tokens are also revoked at the
      platform, or 30 days after Pro ends. Message ids for skipping duplicates live in memory only.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Dashboard from anywhere</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What:</strong> for each phone or mod you add, its id, the PC it belongs to, its role
      (owner or mod), the name you gave it, a hash of its sign-in and when it was created, last used
      and expires. An unused invite link is kept as a hash for 10 minutes. A short activity log
      records each change made from a phone: the kind of action, the result, the device and the
      time, never what was sent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Why:</strong> so only devices you approved can reach your dashboard, and you can see
      what they changed.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Passing through only:</strong> requests and answers between your phone and your PC,
      and the live feed, are held in the relay’s memory only while they pass through. When your PC
      is off, bans and timeouts made from a phone wait on the relay until your PC picks them up.
      Moderation details such as reasons are never stored. A Twitch access token for moderation is
      held in memory for up to an hour.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long:</strong> the activity log for 30 days. A device until you remove it, which
      you can do at any time, and at most 30 days after Pro ends. A phone’s sign-in also stops
      working after 30 days without use.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Ferrocast voices</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What:</strong> a count of characters read this month for your subscription, and one
      total a month for all of Pro together. Never the text, the voice or the audio.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Why:</strong> to keep within the monthly limit. Only lines that passed your own
      approval and filters are sent. Their text goes to Google Cloud Text-to-Speech to make the
      audio, which passes back to your PC and is not kept on the relay.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long:</strong> the monthly counts, deleted with the rest after Pro ends.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Discord bot</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What:</strong> your server’s id, name and icon, the channel for go-live posts, your
      go-live switch and message, a random link code and your role rules. The last go-live post per
      platform, for 30 days. For each role given: the Discord user, role, rule and end date.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Viewers who link Discord:</strong> a viewer can choose to link their Discord account
      to get a role. We keep only their Discord user id and the ids of the Twitch or YouTube
      accounts Discord has verified for them. Never their names or email. Discord’s sign-in token is
      revoked right after we read those ids.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Why:</strong> to post when you go live and give the right roles.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long:</strong> until you disconnect the server, or 30 days after Pro ends. A
      viewer can ask us to delete their link at any time.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Cloud backups</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What:</strong> the encrypted backup file, plus its id, which of your PCs uploaded it,
      its size, a checksum of the encrypted file, the app version, whether it was automatic or
      manual, and dates.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Encrypted on your PC:</strong> the backup is locked on your computer before upload.
      The key stays in your PC’s secure storage, and your recovery key and optional passphrase are
      never sent to us. We cannot open a backup.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Why:</strong> so you can restore your setup on this PC or another one.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long:</strong> until you delete it or a newer one replaces it (7 backups at most).
      Unfinished uploads are deleted after a day. All backups are deleted 30 days after Pro ends,
      and you can still download them until then.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Stream history and weekly email</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What:</strong> for each stream and platform, its start and end, title, category, peak
      and average viewers, and totals for chat lines, chatters, new chatters, follows, subs and
      tips. A viewer count every 5 minutes while you are live. Only counts: never chat, viewer names
      or who watched.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Weekly email:</strong> your email address, sealed, plus a keyed fingerprint of it for
      unsubscribe links. Its status, when it was saved and confirmed, and the confirmation link’s
      hash and expiry. When each week’s report went, for 120 days. The email is built from your
      history when it is sent and is not stored. Brevo sends it.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Why:</strong> to show your stream history and send the weekly report you asked for.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long:</strong> history while you have Pro, up to 400 days, then 30 days after Pro
      ends. Your email address goes as soon as you stop the emails or unsubscribe, a week after an
      unconfirmed link expires, or 30 days after Pro ends.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Tip page upgrades</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>What:</strong> your three page colours and your avatar and banner. Images are redrawn
      from their pixels, so location and camera details are removed. A tip goal’s title, target,
      currency and dates. For each tip counted toward a goal, only its amount and a one-way
      fingerprint of the payment, never the tipper’s name, message or payment id.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Your own address:</strong> the address, its Cloudflare id and status, the verification
      records and when the proof was last seen. Nothing about visitors.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Why:</strong> to show your tip page and goal in your style and at your address.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>How long:</strong> a goal’s tip records 60 days after the goal ends. Colours, images
      and goals 30 days after Pro ends. Your own address 7 days after Pro ends, or 7 days after it
      stops working, and then it is also removed from Cloudflare.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <p>
    ferrocast.clearcraftlabs.com is a static site. It sets no cookies and loads nothing from other
    companies: fonts and images are served from the same address. It stores one setting in your
    browser, your light or dark theme choice, which never leaves your device. Our hosting provider
    may keep standard server logs (IP address, page, time) for security, for a short period.
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell or rent personal data, and we do not use it for advertising. We share data only
    with the services needed to run what you ask for (hosting for the relay, Razorpay for Pro
    payments) or when the law requires it.
  </p>
  <p>
    For Pro, these companies process data for us, each only for a feature you turned on, and each
    receives only what that feature needs:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Razorpay</strong>: Pro payments and subscriptions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google Cloud Text-to-Speech</strong>: the text of lines read by Ferrocast voices.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Brevo</strong>: sends the weekly email and its confirmation email.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong>: carries the connection to your phone dashboard, sets up and
      secures custom tip addresses, and answers the DNS check for them.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Discord</strong>: go-live posts and roles in your server.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Twitch and Kick</strong>: the cloud bot’s messages and moderation.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>Each one handles data under its own privacy policy.</p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask us what data we hold about you, ask us to correct or delete it, and withdraw consent
    at any time. Users in India have these rights under the Digital Personal Data Protection Act,
    2023; users in the EU and UK have them under the GDPR. Write to
    <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.privacyEmail}`}>{COMPANY.privacyEmail}</a> and we will answer within
    {COMPANY.responseDays} working days and act within 30 days.
  </p>

  <h2>Age</h2>
  <p>
    Ferrocast’s hosted services (the relay, tip pages and Pro) are for people aged 18 or over. If
    you are under 18, you may use them only with the consent of a parent or lawful guardian, who
    agrees to this policy for you. We do not knowingly process a child’s data without that consent.
    Streaming platforms also set their own age limits.
  </p>

  <h2>Grievance officer</h2>
  <p>
    For complaints under Indian law, contact our grievance officer: {COMPANY.grievanceOfficer.name},
    <a href={`mailto:${COMPANY.grievanceOfficer.email}`}>{COMPANY.grievanceOfficer.email}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes in a way that matters, we will update the date at the top and note the
    change in the app’s release notes.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <Address />
</Legal>
